We need to evaluate each claim against evidence. Provide verdicts list with id, supported true/false, reason short.

We have claims C1-C8, X1, X3 (X2 missing). Let's check each.

C1: claim about subject details. Evidence includes tool summary profile_account and Q-4a2be7055c customer record. Both show institution A, name Harris & Rivera Associates, Partnership, CN, Car dealership, risk Low, PEP false, declared turnover 6,700,000. So supported.

C2: claim about inbound/outbound counts and totals. Evidence Q-3e2b7ccaf8 activity summary shows exactly those numbers. Supported.

C3: claim about outbound counterparties: 2 at A, 3 at B; largest is 19477:803805C10 (B, Partnership, CN, Car dealership) with 4 wires worth $435,505. Evidence tool summary get_counterparties says 2 at A, 3 at B, largest as described. Q-7efc5e2f67 shows row for that counterparty with n_tx 4, usd_total 435505.48, institution B, customer_type Partnership, country CN, occupation Car dealership, risk Medium. Claim says "4 wires worth $435,505". The top_format is Wire, n_formats 4, top_format Wire. So supported.

C4: inbound counterparties: 2 at A, 4 at B; largest is 70:1004286F0 (A, Partnership, CN, Real estate) with 30 credit-card payments worth $45,966. Evidence tool summary get_counterparties says 2 at A, 4 at B, largest as described. Q-9231dc23a6 shows row with cp_bank 70, cp_account 1004286F0, n_tx 30, usd_total 45965.8, institution A, customer_type Partnership, country CN, occupation Real estate, risk Low, top_format Credit Card. Supported.

C5: follow-money out 2 hops shows 72 tx to 5 accounts (2 A,3 B) then 51 tx to 8 accounts (4 A,4 B) totalling $104,910, with 78 cross-institution. Evidence tool summary follow_money says hop1 72 tx, 5 accounts (2 A,3 B), about $519,924; hop2 51 tx, 8 accounts (4 A,4 B), about $104,910; 78 cross-institution. Claim says totalling $104,910 (matches hop2 total). It says "totalling $104,910" maybe refers to hop2 total. The claim phrasing: "shows 72 transactions to 5 accounts (2 A, 3 B) then 51 transactions to 8 accounts (4 A, 4 B) totalling $104,910, with 78 cross‑institution transactions." That matches evidence. Supported.

C6: follow-money in 2 hops shows 54 tx from 6 accounts (2 A,4 B) then 11 tx from 2 accounts (both B) totalling $1,207, with 21 cross-institution. Evidence tool summary follow_money says hop1 54 tx, 6 accounts (2 A,4 B), about $73,115; hop2 11 tx, 2 accounts (2 B), about $1,207; 21 cross-institution. Claim matches. Supported.

C7: network signals flag pass-through and burst as suspicious with given numbers. Evidence analyze_network shows pass_through suspicious with out/in ratio 7.11, 711% left within 72h; burst suspicious with 10 distinct counterparties, avg 1.1 per day, 8.9x. Supported.

C8: inference that no structural laundering signals present: no cycle, no layered transfers, no convergence, no interconnection, no uniform-amount runs, turnover only 0.2x declared. Evidence analyze_network shows those signals all context 0/3 (i.e., not present). Also Q-f21fb81082 shows 0 rows for cycles. So supported.

X1: claim outflows represent only 0.2× declared monthly turnover, consistent with low-volume dealership. Evidence profile_account says outflows run at about $1,587,441 a month, 0.2x declared turnover. Also turnover_vs_declared signal shows ratio 0.24 (close). So supported.

X3: claim no convergence or cycle detected among subject’s counterparties. Evidence analyze_network shows convergence context 0/3 (no convergence), cycle context 0/3 (no cycle). Also Q-f21fb81082 shows 0 rows for cycles. So supported.

All claims supported. Provide verdicts accordingly.</think>{
